<% layout("layouts/boilerplate") -%>

<main class="py-4 py-lg-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <article class="col-lg-9 col-xl-8">
            <header class="mb-4 pb-3 border-bottom">
                <p class="text-danger fw-semibold text-uppercase small mb-2">Legal</p>
                <h1 class="display-6 fw-semibold mb-2">Privacy policy</h1>
                <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">Last updated: October 12, 2026</p>
            </header>

            <div class="alert alert-light border" role="note">
                This independent learning project does not process bookings or payments. This policy describes the information used by the features currently available on Heavenly.
            </div>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">1. Who operates this site</h2>
                <p>Heavenly is an independent project. The person or team operating the specific deployment controls the information described here. This site is not affiliated with Airbnb.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">2. Information used by the site</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> username, email address, and password authentication data. The authentication library stores password credentials in hashed form; the application does not need your plain-text password after sign-in.</li>
                    <li><strong>Listing content:</strong> titles, descriptions, nightly prices, country and city details, map coordinates, and uploaded photos.</li>
                    <li><strong>Reviews and saved stays:</strong> review ratings and comments, plus the listing IDs you save to your account.</li>
                    <li><strong>Basic technical data:</strong> an essential session cookie used to keep you signed in, search terms included in the page URL, and diagnostic information created while the operator maintains the site.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Do not enter payment card details or other sensitive information; the current project has no checkout or payment feature.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">3. How information appears and is used</h2>
                <p>Account information is used to sign you in and provide account features. Saved stays are associated with your account and are shown in your saved list. Listing details, photos, and map locations are visible to visitors. Reviews and ratings are visible with the reviewer’s username.</p>
                <p>The operator may use submitted information to run, maintain, secure, and improve this project, respond to issues, and address misuse. The current application does not include advertising or analytics tracking.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">4. Service providers and sharing</h2>
                <p>Information and listing records, including default photo URLs, are stored in MongoDB Atlas. Default photos load from Unsplash; photos uploaded by hosts are stored with Cloudinary. Map display and location lookup use Mapbox; a location entered for a listing is sent to Mapbox to find map coordinates. These providers may process technical information such as your network address when your browser or the server contacts them, under their own privacy terms.</p>
                <p>If you choose a social sharing link, your browser sends the public Heavenly page link to the social network you selected. Heavenly does not control how that network uses information.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">5. Cookies, sessions, and logs</h2>
                <p>The site uses an essential session cookie for login and account features. The current demo keeps session state in server memory, so sessions may end when they expire or the server restarts. No advertising or analytics cookies are configured by this application.</p>
                <p>Diagnostic output may contain account or listing details used to troubleshoot the app. The deployment operator can access server logs and should protect them appropriately.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">6. Retention and your choices</h2>
                <p>Information remains in the project while the relevant account or content remains in its database or provider storage. You can remove saved stays, delete your own reviews, or delete listings you own using the available controls. This version does not have a self-service account deletion feature. Deleted content may remain in logs, backups, or third-party storage for a time.</p>
                <p>Depending on the privacy laws where you live, you may have rights to request access, correction, or deletion. Contact the person or team operating this deployment to make a request.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">7. Security and children</h2>
                <p>The operator uses the safeguards available in this project, but no website or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure. This demo is not designed to collect information from children.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">8. Updates and questions</h2>
                <p>We may update this policy as the project’s features or data practices change. The latest update date is shown at the top of this page. For privacy questions or requests, contact the person or team operating the Heavenly deployment.</p>
                <p class="mb-0">See the <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a> for rules covering use of the site.</p>
            </section>
        </article>
    </div>
</main>
